# D-FREED-INODE-HOME-NEVER-PUBLISHED-LIVE-CORE-AFTER-CLEAN-UNMOUNT, H-F12 with
# reach.  tests/queues/pub_drain_bound_ab.queue (pb) ran H-F12's same-build A/B
# on lap fds3's settings with NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200; its laps were VACUOUS
# because node A (test1, the churner) received 0 or 1 AG release request after
# each lap's mark (fds1-fds4 the same: one per lap).  In multi-node every file
# and directory is allocated in its creating node's own AG
# (xfs/libxfs/xfs_ialloc.c xfs_dialloc_pick_ag), so a peer asks for A's churn AG
# essentially only when it frees one of A's inodes as their last closer, and the
# stat/touch lookup loop makes the peer the last closer rarely.  The claim delay
# makes every request that meets A's churn a chase, but makes no requests.
#
# REACH KNOB: NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 makes the lookup loop also hold each file
# open for 50 ms (tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh): when A removes a file B is holding,
# B becomes its last closer, frees it, and asks A for A's churn AG while A is
# creating in it, which is H-F12's case.  Everything else is pb's line.
#
# Same-build A/B, one knob between the arms: pub_drain_bound (1 bounds an AG
# release's drain to the entries listed when it began; 0 is the open scan),
# set and read back on every node by NG0_DRAIN_BOUND.  Build: ~/src/mxfs-b, the
# H-F12 change plus a read-only instrument at every AG unlock, both arms
# (xfs/xfs_mxfs_publish.c mxfs_pub_unlock_exposure, line P-PUB-UNPUB-AT-UNLOCK,
# counters pub_unlock_exposed and pub_unlock_listed), and the phantom detector's
# snapshot of the inode's unpublished state and in-flight claim taken before it
# asks the DLM (xfs/libxfs/xfs_trans_inode.c: q_inflight, q_us, requery; read
# only); its srcversion is printed by each lap.  Run from ~/src/mxfs-b, whose harness refuses a node running
# anything else.  Control and fix laps alternate, control first, on
# 3/net/mesh/direct g3 (test1 test2 test3).
#
# MEASURES, per lap (RESULT line; each node's whole kernel log after the mark):
#   dt_ag, dt_dir, stuck_chase, stuck_held, pc_rel_ag, pc_rel_dir, db_left:
#     as in pb's queue
#   ux_unlocks   AG unlocks (site=ag-bast) with an unpublished inode of that AG
#                still listed or its claim in flight (P-PUB-UNPUB-AT-UNLOCK)
#   ux_listed / ux_unlinked / ux_inflight   summed over those lines: listed
#                inodes of the AG, of them already unlinked, claims in flight
#   audit, node_failures, and every other gate the harness applies
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   A lap with a node failure or a CORRUPT cold audit is attributed before
#   anything below is judged.  A lap whose audit is STALE/NONE, or an ABORT, has
#   no verdict and is rerun.  The harness's VACUOUS (control: dt_ag 0; fix:
#   db_left 0 and dt_ag 0) did not reach and judges nothing.
#   H-F12, unchanged from pb's rules:
#     CONTROL (bound 0), reached: SHOWS THE CAUSE if its AG drain timeouts'
#       STUCK lines are chase-shaped (stuck_chase > 0, stuck_held 0); only held
#       STUCK lines REFUTE H-F12 for them.
#     FIX (bound 1), reached: PASS if dt_ag 0, pc_rel_ag 0, cold audit CLEAN
#       errors=0, node_failures 0 and every other harness gate holds.  A reached
#       fix lap with an AG drain timeout REFUTES H-F12.
#     A failure only through the directory scope is its own finding.
#     SUPPORTED AND FIXED: at least one control SHOWS THE CAUSE and at least
#       two reached fix laps PASS, with no reached fix lap failing on the AG
#       scope.  WEAK: the controls do not reach: more control laps.
#   THE HANDOFF EXPOSURE (the consult's question; it judges H-F12's
#   completeness, not its verdict above):
#     EXPOSED   any reached fix lap with ux_listed > 0: a bounded AG release
#               handed the AG off with unpublished inodes of that AG listed.
#               With ux_unlinked > 0 among them, the inodes a peer's
#               unlinked-list remove can take as predecessor were among them.
#               H-F12 is then not the complete fix, and the AG handoff needs an
#               enrollment fence (the next hypothesis) whatever H-F12's verdict.
#     The control arm's ux fields are read the same way: they say what the
#     open scan leaves at a handoff today.
#     NOT SEEN  every reached lap of both arms ux_unlocks 0.
#
# Bound: fw3's, 1680 s per lap (pb's laps 494-519 s).
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=0 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brc1 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brf1 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=0 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brc2 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brf2 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=0 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brc3 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
1680 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots NG0_LOOKUP_HOLD_MS=50 NG0_DRAIN_BOUND=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_GUARD=1 NG0_PUBCLAIM_DELAY_MS=200 NG0_CREATE_PARENT_DELAY_MS=5 NG0_SELFCLOBBER_GUARD=1 NG0_MIRROR_CHECK=1 NG0_RECYCLE_GUARD=1 NG0_FRESHSRC_GUARD=1 NG0_DELAY_MS=0 NG0_IFREE_DRAIN=1 NG0_IFREE_REAP=1 tests/noino_gen0_ab.sh brf3 1 300 3/net/mesh/direct g3
